<%# locals: (page: nil, title_action: nil) %>
<%# The head of the API tokens (Mein Konto › API-Tokens), on the list and on every
    page below it: the shared page head (organisations/shared/_subnav) titled by the
    area, as every area's pages are. A page below the list (a new token, a rename,
    the token just created) keeps this head and names itself in the crumb line
    (organisations/shared/_section_crumb), with the way back to the list.

    Until 2026-11-12 each of the four pages built a title box of its own, under a top
    gap of its own (pt-6) and with a title of its own. %>
<%= render 'organisations/shared/subnav',
      title: t('navigation.settings_api_tokens'),
      aria_label: t('navigation.settings_api_tokens'),
      active: nil,
      tabs: [],
      title_action: title_action %>
<% if page.present? %>
  <%= render 'organisations/shared/section_crumb',
        back_label: t('navigation.settings_api_tokens'),
        back_path: users_personal_access_tokens_path,
        page: page %>
<% end %>
